le","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-anxiety-and-general-anxiety-group/events/312664391/","description":"Our coffee shop meetup now takes place every other Saturday. Come out to meet and chat with your fellow members of the Toronto Social Anxiety Support group in a supportive environment.\n\n**IMPORTANT: This group is intended to provide a safe space for people with social anxiety who may feel inhibited in louder, more extroverted environments. Please respect the nature of this group and do not attend if you are not in this category. There are many other groups available on Meetup.**\n\n**When**: 5pm - 7pm\n\n**Where to meet**: Alternity Café, just west of St. George Street, on the south side of Bloor. Vegan café with a chill vibe. Here is their website: https://alternity.ca/pages/our-place\n\n**Reminder**: Like all our events, the group's code of conduct applies. Pls make this a successful outing by being courteous and respectful in language and behaviour, and supportive towards other members, especially those with higher anxiety.\n\n**Covid/flu safety**: If you are sick or have recently been exposed to someone who is sick, pls use your judgement about attending this event. You can always come to the next event when you feel better.","startDate":"2026-10-24T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Alternity","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"333 Bloor st west Toronto,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Shyness, Social Anxiety and General Anxiety Support Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/social-anxiety-and-general-anxiety-group/"},"performer":"Shyness, Social Anxiety and General Anxiety Support Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🤝 Fast Friends: Meet New People & Make New Friends | Board Games | 25–45","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/events/316744703/","description":"You can live in a city full of people and still wonder, “Where do I actually meet new friends?”\n\nFast Friends makes that first step easy. Meet over 25 new people through relaxed, guided conversations, discover shared interests and then stay for drinks and board games with the people you click with.\n\n🎲 Stout has 50+ board games to enjoy after the hosted rounds, plus an After Dark Special from 9–11 PM with $7 beers and $7 highballs.\n\n🎟️ Book Online & Save: [https://toronto24thoct.eventbrite.co.uk](https://toronto24thoct.eventbrite.co.uk)\nEarly Bird: CAD $10\nRegular: CAD $15\nAt the Door: CAD $20 cash — to host Kruttika\nBooking in advance helps us plan the right space and group size and guarantees your place.\n\n🍻 What to Expect\n7:00 PM – Welcome & Drinks\nMeet your host, Kruttika, grab a drink and settle in.\nComing alone? Most people do! Our host will welcome you, make introductions and help you feel comfortable.\n\n🤝 7:30 PM – Fast Friends\nMeet a variety of friendly people through short, guided conversations.\nNo awkwardly approaching strangers — we guide the conversations and rotations, so you can simply focus on getting to know people.\n\n🎲 From 8:30 PM – Board Games & Mingling\nThe hosted rounds finish, but the evening doesn't have to.\nStay for drinks, play some easy social board games with the people you've met, or simply continue chatting and getting to know your new connections.\n\n❤️ Why People Love Fast Friends\n✔ Meet over 25 new people in one evening\n✔ No awkwardly approaching strangers — we guide the conversations\n✔ Most attendees come solo\n✔ Friendly hosts and a welcoming atmosphere\n✔ Common Ground Challenge to discover shared interests\n✔ Easy board games & socialising after the hosted rounds\n✔ Relaxed pub setting\n✔ Friendship-focused — not a dating event\n\n👥 Who Is This For?\n✔ Ages 25–45\n✔ New to Toronto or long-time locals\n✔ Solo attendees welcome\n✔ Anyone looking to make new friends and expand their social circle\nWe're not a closed group — new faces are always welcome, and you'll never feel like an outsider.\n\n💳 Why We Use Tickets\nYour ticket helps us:\n• Organise the right venue space\n• Support our local hosts\n• Create a safer, more committed group experience\n• Deliver a well-organised evening for everyone\n\n🌍 About Fast Friends\nFor over 10 years, Fast Friends has been helping people meet new people and build meaningful friendships in 30+ cities around the world.\n\nOur mission is simple:\nTo make meeting new people easy, relaxed and enjoyable.\nCome solo. Start with one conversation. Leave with new friends. ❤️","startDate":"2026-10-24T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Stout Irish pub","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"221 Carlton St., Toronto, ON M5A 2L2, Canada,, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-singles-in-the-city/"},"performer":"Toronto Singles in the city (13000+)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto’s BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event Party + Bonus Class by [TILE.]","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tilesocial/events/316668944/","description":"**Join [TILE.]** at the **most popular Saturday Language Learning Social Event & Party in Toronto! 🍁**\n\n**[TILE.] = Toronto International Language Exchange [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/tilelearning/) & [Website](https://www.tilelearning.com/)**\n\n**[TILE.]** now has a **2-for-1 special event,** which includes:\n**1.** F