e Social Event + Class"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Brunch at Solena Brunch Bar - Saturday, October 24th, 2026 @11:00 AM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-over-50-meetup-group/events/316743063/","description":"Hi Ladies,\nCome enjoy a delicious brunch with a Mediterranean twist on **Saturday**, October 24th, 2026 at **11:00 AM** at Solena Brunch Bar. The venue offers a wonderful variety of brunch options and beverage selections. Vegan choices are also available. The restaurant is bright and tastefully decorated with attentive waitstaff. The gratuity will be automatically added. Click [here](https://www.solenabrunch.ca/menu) for a link to the brunch menu. Meet friends and make some new ones while enjoying a lovely Brunch. Each participant will cover their own food and drink costs.\n**There is a non-refundable / non-transferable $5.00 cover fee** to attend this group event. This charge will reserve your spot, help with group costs and hopefully minimize no shows. **Payment of the $5 cover charge is due by FRIDAY, OCTOBER 16th, 2026.** After this date, non payment of the cover fee will result in the Member's name being moved to the \"not going\" list so that those \"waitlisted\" have an opportunity to attend the Brunch.\nIn consideration of others, if you are not able to attend, please advise 48 hours prior to the event to allow other people on the waitlist to have your spot. No shows and less than 48 hours notice of non-attendance will be noted. 2 or more such occurrences will unfortunately lead to removal from the group. Thank you all for your understanding and consideration. Looking forward to connecting soon!\nHere are the details for the $5.00 e-transfer - E-mail - [weekendbrunchover50@hotmail.com](http://weekendbrunchover50@hotmail.com/), Security Question - What is the time of the event? **Eleven**\nHope to see you there!","startDate":"2026-10-24T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"SOLENA Brunch & Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1224 St Clair Ave W, Toronto, ON M6E 1B4, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Weekend Brunch and More for Ladies Over 50 (Ladies Only)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-over-50-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Weekend Brunch and More for Ladies Over 50 (Ladies Only)"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Founders and Entrepreneurs Networking at 5 Elements Espresso Bar","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-founders-hub/events/315547599/","description":"Join the Toronto Founders Hub every other Saturday at 3:30pm for our regular meetup at 5 Elements Espresso Bar.\n\nSit down with other entrepreneurs to network and discuss business ideas or strategies.\n\\- Broaden your network\n\\- Get critical feedback\n\\- Socialize in low pressure setting\n\nI look forward to seeing you!","startDate":"2026-10-24T19:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"5 Elements Espresso","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"131 Avenue Road, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Founders and Entrepreneurs Hub","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-founders-hub/"},"performer":"Toronto Founders and Entrepreneurs Hub"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fall colors walk / hike at Earl Bales park ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/events/316683588/","description":"Lets go for a hike/walk at the trails of Earl Bales park and the nearby trails. We will wait 15 mins for people to show up and then start walking at 12:15pm.\n\nDifficulty - Easy (with some uphill/downhill)\n\nDistance - 4 to 7km (Will adjust distance based on weather and trail conditions)\n\n**Meeting Spot**\nEarl Bales Community Center\n[https://goo.gl/maps/bN29TZPwFtUQCKE8A](https://goo.gl/maps/bN29TZPwFtUQCKE8A)\n\n**Free Parking**\nThere are multiple parking lots in this park, some closer and some further from the meeting spot.\n\n**TTC**\nGet off at Sheppard & Bathurst and walk 5 mins to meeting spot.\n\n**SOCIAL**\n***Join Whatsapp Group - [CLICK HERE](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSflzD3fDrU5sLARAT5yDF3OhEu3Vj-2P7ci8mP5FYX46rt1NQ/viewform)***\n***[Follow on Instagram - CLICK HERE](https://www.instagram.com/tam.club/)***","startDate":"2026-10-24T16:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Earl Bales Community Center","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"4169 Bathurst St, North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"All-Level &Beginner Friendly $10 Drop In Saturday Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332816/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\n\\*The close intersection in Birchmount Rd & Lawrence Ave.\nTime: Saturday 9:30 AM - 12 PM\n\\*\\*\\*9:30 AM- 12 PM 3 courts available\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\\*Please bring your own racquet,\n\\*Please bring indoor gym sport shoes. (Change shoes in the club)\n\\*\\*\\*\n\\*This weekly gathering is for all levels (beginner to advance) badminton players.\n\\*No outside food allowed.\n\\* This event is for the purpose of playing friendly double games and for all levels of players from beginner to advance. Please do not use this as an opportunity to do training and singles games.\nAttendance in effect -please give at least 24hr notice in advance for cancelation so others may have time to react. Late show and no-shows maybe permanently removed from group and unable to rejoin.\n\\*Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-10-24T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Christian Imagination and the Question of Autonomous Art","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/events/316585615/","description":"[Theopolis](https://www.theopolis.ca/) is excited to present the inaugural Gaudí Lecture, featuring renowned liturgical artist, writer, and speaker Jonathan Pageau.\n\nThe notion of “art for art’s sake” continues to pervade contemporary thinking and practice in the arts. Art is understood as autonomous, liberated from its connection to worship, culture, morality, truth, or beauty, or reduced to a commodity valued primarily for its price and prestige. In either case, art risks becoming detached from the larger human story.\n\nIn this lecture, Pageau will argue that the response of the Christian imagination is not simply to reunite art with religious content by depicting biblical scenes or communicating moral messages. Rather, liturgy and sacramentality must be recovered as the internal and coherent driving force of the arts themselves, shaping their forms and their application within the Body of Christ.\n\n**Please note this is a ticketed event. YOU NEED TO PURCHASE A TICKET IN ADVANCE through this link [HERE](https://www.theopolis.ca/gaudi-lecture/) to be admitted. Theopolis has generously offered a package of 10 discounted (25% off) tickets for members of the Toronto Philosophy Meetup — use the code TPM2026 at checkout to receive the discount.**\n\n***______________________________________________***\n\nABOUT JONATHAN PAGEAU\n\nJonathan Pageau is a renowned liturgical artist, writer, and public speaker whose work explores symbolism, religion, art, literature, and culture.\n\nThrough his carvings, writing, lectures, and *The Symbolic World*, Pageau has helped a wide audience recover a symbolic vision of the world, one in which spiritual meaning is revealed through images, stories, rituals, and the patterns of everyday life. Drawing deeply from the Christian tradition, his work offers a compelling way of engaging many of the central questions facing contemporary culture.\n\nTheopolis is honoured to welcome Jonathan Pageau to Toronto to deliver the inaugural Gaudí Lecture.\n\n***______________________________________________***\n\nABOUT THEOPOLIS\n\nCatholic art has the power to renew culture and share the faith through beauty, but in Ontario, it’s too often absent from public life. Theopolis exists to change that. We’re empowering a rising generation of Catholic artists and creating a space for encounter between the secular and sacred.\n\nWe believe that art plays a vital role in shaping how we understand the world, and that beauty can serve as an avenue for the Holy Spirit — sparking an encounter with the sacred. By bringing works of Catholic art into dialogue with contemporary Canadian culture, Theopolis ensures that the Catholic imagination remains part of the public conversation, creating spaces where culture and faith meet.\n\nMore info about Theopolis here: https://www.theopolis.ca/about/\n\n***______________________________________________***\n\nABOUT THE GAUDÍ LECTURE\n\nThe Gaudí Lecture is an annual public lecture exploring the importance, influence, and enduring relevance of the Christian imagination. Each year, Theopolis will invite a distinguished creative figure to reflect on the role of the Christian imagination in shaping culture, artistic practice, and daily life.\n\nThe lecture is named for Venerable Antoni Gaudí, whose architecture reflects an imagination formed by faith, nature, craftsmanship, and a profound sense of the sacred. His work reveals how artistic practice can become a form of contemplation and how beauty can prepare the soul for faith.\n\nThrough this series, Theopolis hopes to create a lasting forum for serious and accessible public conversation, bringing artists, students, professionals, clergy, patrons, academics, and members of the wider community into a shared exploration of art, faith, and culture.","startDate":"2026-10-24T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Northrop Frye Hall (University of Toronto) Room NF003","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"73 Queen’s Park Cres. E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-toronto-philosophy-meetup/"},"performer":"The Toronto Philosophy Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"ARTbus: Mississauga and Oakville Galleries ($20)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/316721528/","description":"Can you join us on our next ARTbus ?? !!\n\nWe've been attending these **ARTbus** trips for many years. Not always able to get them posted on MEETUP-as they fill up quite quickly.\n\n$20 ticket link is below.\n\n***Purchase your OWN ticket*** when you RSVP on Meetup.\n\n**In partnership with the Art Gallery of Mississauga, Oakville Galleries invites you to join us for the FALL 2026 ARTbus.**\n\n(We rent a BUS--ok its a **yellow school bus**--but it works!) Hence the $20 price!\n\n**$20 per person** at the *link below. (By signing up--signals to me that you've purchased your $20 ticket--LET me know via Meetup email)*\n\nWould you like to join in this next one/upcoming? **Saturday October 24th. (11am-5:30pm)**\n\nThis will be incredible afternoon!! International artists. Lovely reception and opening comments.\n\n**We'll begin** the afternoon at a Gallery opening at Bloor/Lansdowne, before heading to Mississauga and Oakville\n\nLet someone else DRIVE while we enjoy socializing and ART learning.\n\n**Reserve your own seat ($20)** and enjoy an inspiring afternoon across three leading art institutions.\n\nWe finish the day at Gairloch Gardens--(right on Lake Ontario) and a nice reception for us (wine/cheese)\n\nhttps://www.oakvillegalleries.com/visit\n\n**TICKET link here (with all details)--**\n\nhttps://www.oakvillegalleries.com/artbus_2026_fall\n\nPlease be on TIME. Plan ahead.\n\nYou should be inside the first gallery by 11:15am. BUS will leave at 12 noon.\n\nSee you there.","startDate":"2026-10-24T15:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Patel Brown","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"21 Wade Ave Unit 2, Toronto, ON M6H 1P4, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/"},"performer":"TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto’s Largest Ecommerce Networking Event – 2 Year Anniversary Party✨","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontoecomnetwork/events/316787151/","description":"***Tickets must be purchased in advance:***\nhttps://luma.com/ecomTO2610?utm_source=meetup\n***(limited early bird & discounted tickets available)***\n\\-\\-\\-\n​**Ecom Network is turning TWO! 🎉** What started as a small meetup in Toronto has grown into a community of more than **4,000 ecommerce founders, operators, and entrepreneurs** \\- and that’s a reason to celebrate\\! 🚀\n\nJoin us for a special **2 Year Anniversary celebration** as we bring the Toronto ecommerce community together for an unforgettable night of networking, drinks, music, and great conversations. 🥂 Most importantly, this night is our way of saying **THANK YOU** to everyone who has supported Ecom Network, attended our events, and helped us build this incredible community over the past two years. ❤️\n\n[Follow us on Instagram @Ecomnetworking](https://instagram.com/ecomnetworking)\n\\-\\-\\-\n**​​Who is this event for?**\nThis event is suitable for all online sellers - whether you run a Direct-to-Consumer (DTC) brand on Shopify, sell on Amazon (FBA), Etsy, eBay, Walmart, or manage a store on social media platforms like Instagram, Facebook, or TikTok.​\n\n—\n**Event Highlights**\n\n**✨ Network in a Vibrant Setting**\nWe’ve secured a dedicated section at at the venue just for our group. Enjoy meaningful conversations and great vibes while connecting with fellow entrepreneurs. We kindly ask that you support the venue by purchasing at least one drink or food item.\n\n📣 **Share Your Story**\nBuilding a brand, product, or project? Looking for partners, feedback, or fresh ideas? This is your chance to introduce yourself and spark valuable connections in the ecommerce community.\n\n💡**Learn and Grow**\nExchange insights on scaling, marketing, operations, and sales with fellow ecommerce founders. Many past attendees have walked away with partnerships, new clients, and fresh ideas - one conversation could be the start of something big.\n\n—\n**Dress code: Smart/Business casual**\n—\nHave questions or suggestions?\n​Feel free to reach out to the organizers!\n​We can’t wait to see you (again)!\n—\n*Notice of Photography*\n*​During the event, photos and videos may be taken for promotional purposes. By attending, you consent to being photographed and/or filmed. If you prefer not to appear in any media, please let one of the event organizers know.*","startDate":"2026-10-24T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Oria on King","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"220 King St W, Toronto, ON M5V 3M2, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Ecom Network","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontoecomnetwork/"},"performer":"Toronto Ecom Network"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park and  Picnic🌳","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316183314/","description":"# 🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park 🌳🍁\n\n### A Real Hike, Beautiful Fall Colours & a Picnic Together\n\nWant to get out of the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\n**Rouge National Urban Park** is Canada's only urban national park — and one of the most popular hikes we do.\nOnce you get onto the trail, it can be hard to believe you're still in Toronto. Forest paths, rolling hills, changing leaves, and quiet stretches of wilderness make this feel much more like a trip outside the city than a walk through it.\nAnd fall is one of the best times to experience it.\n\nThis is **a real hike**, though. There are some hills and ups and downs, so it isn't the best choice if you're looking for an easy, flat walk.\nBut if you're up for the challenge, there's something satisfying about reaching the end knowing you did it together.\nAnd then we'll have a picnic. 🧺\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🥾 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet at **Don Mills Station** and take the 85C bus together toward Rouge National Urban Park.\nOnce we arrive, we'll begin our hike through the park.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Hike through forest and open spaces 🌳\n* Enjoy the fall colours 🍂\n* Navigate the hills and changing terrain\n* Take in some beautiful views\n* Stop for a short break along the route\n* Finish at the Park's Welcome Centre\n* Have a **30–40 minute group picnic** afterward 🧺\n\nThe hike takes approximately **2½ hours**, plus a short break.\nAfterward, we'll take some time to relax, eat, and enjoy each other's company.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is a **moderately challenging hike**, not a casual stroll.\nThere are hills, uneven sections, and some ups and downs, so good walking or hiking shoes are important.\nPlease come prepared for typical fall weather and bring enough water for the hike.\n\nIf you're comfortable walking for a couple of hours and handling some elevation changes, you'll be fine.\nIf you're looking for something completely flat and easy, **this probably isn't the walk for you.**\n\n***\n\n## 🚌 Meetup Details\n\n### 🚇 By TTC\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Don Mills Station — on the platform for the **85C bus**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **9:45 AM**\n🚌 **Bus Leaves:** **10:06 AM sharp**\nI'll wait for the bus, but if you miss it, **you won't be able to join the group afterward.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n\n### 🚗 By Car\n\nParking is **not available at our TTC meeting point.**\n\nIf you're driving, please park at the **Toronto Zoo** and walk to the **Park's Welcome Centre (the house)**.\n🚗 **Car Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM\n\nWe may be a few minutes late arriving, depending on the bus and traffic.\n\n***\n\n## 🧺 The Picnic\n\nAfter the hike, we'll have a **30–40 minute group picnic** at the end.\nPlease bring something small to share — nothing too large or heavy. The goal is simply to have something to eat together after the hike.\n🥪 Sandwiches\n🍎 Fruit\n🍪 Snacks\n🥤 Drinks\nWhatever is easy to carry and share is perfect.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details at a Glance\n\n🥾 **Hike:** Approximately 2½ hours + short break\n🧺 **Picnic:** 30–40 minutes\n🏁 **End Point:** Park's Welcome Centre\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5 cash or e-transfer\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n🥾 Good walking shoes or hiking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧺 Something small to share for the picnic\n🧥 A fall jacket or layers\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis hike is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy a little challenge\n* Anyone who wants to explore Rouge National Urban Park\n* People who love fall colours 🍂\n* Hikers looking for a social outing\n* Anyone comfortable walking hills and uneven terrain\n* People who want to meet others while getting outside\n\nThis isn't the easiest walk we do.\n**But sometimes the harder walks are the ones you remember.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the hike.**\n**Stay for the picnic.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-24T13:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Don Mills Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1800 Sheppard Avenue East,  M2J 5A7, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/b/6/highres_509641206.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/a/6/b/highres_536350859.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/1/0/5/highres_535717125.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/4/6/0/highres_536365696.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/3/6/3/